      ],
      "text": "**Singapore’s air quality is very poor right now.** The latest readings I found, for **Friday, October 16**, show a **24-hour PSI of 226 in Central Singapore**—“Very Unhealthy”—and **1-hour PM2.5 of 194 µg/m³ in the South**, classified as “High.” Readings vary by region. ([haze.sg](https://www.haze.sg/))\n\nNEA’s forecast for today is **Unhealthy to low Very Unhealthy**. If you’re outside, check the latest **1-hour PM2.5** for your area; NEA advises avoiding strenuous outdoor activity when it’s in the High band, and people with heart or lung conditions, older adults, pregnant people, and children should avoid outdoor activity at that level. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-15-october-2026))",
